Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:18:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Graphs of a predicate-object map: those of the subject map
 and its own

A predicate-object map of a triples map whose subject map has a graph map
generated its triples in the subject map's graphs only; its own graph maps
were ignored. R2RML (11.1) and RML give such triples in the union of both:
RMLTC0009b (CSV, JSON, XML; RMLio/rml-test-cases) expects the practise
triples in both <graph/practise> and <graph/students>.

The graph generator of such a predicate-object map is now the union of the
two. RMLTC0009b moves from the failing test cases to rml-testcases (the
CSV copy now names its sources as the others do).
